    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d410">

                <pb facs="0565" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg459"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Tsui</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-06-17"><hi rendition="#italic">June 17,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 2d instant, and to say in reply that, having made known its
                    contents to the Secretary of the Treasury, he has decided that there are no
                    objections to the acceptance by our customs collectors of the certificates of
                    identity, which, under authority of the Imperial Government, are issued by its
                    consuls in foreign countries to certain Chinese subjects of the exempt class
                    contemplated in section 6 of the act of May 6, 1882, as amended July 5, 1884,
                    and will take action accordingly. I inclose a copy of his letter.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d410-a1.xml" xpointer="d410-a1"/>
            </div>
